<title>USA: 3Com to acquire Onstream Networks.</title>
<headline>3Com to acquire Onstream Networks.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Networking company 3Com Corp said Monday it has signed a definitive agreement to acquire OnStream Networks Inc.</p>
<p>OnStream is a provider of asynchronous transfer mode and broadband wide area network products.</p>
<p>3Com said it plans to exchange 3.8 million shares, and options to purchase its shares, for all outstanding shares and options of OnStream.</p>
<p>Based upon the closing price of Friday's closing price of 3Com the deal is valued at $245 million.</p>
<p>The deal which will be accounted for as a pooling of interests is expected to close November 30, pending regulatory approval.</p>
<p>3Com also said it had signed an agreement that will allow it to immediately purchase and resell OnStream's ATM and other broadband product lines.</p>
</text>
